# Cloudflare Pages redirects — copied verbatim into dist/ by Astro.
#
# Why the bare domain is redirected rather than served
#
# Both https://landedmath.com/ and https://www.landedmath.com/ answered HTTP 200 with identical content,
# so every page existed at two live URLs. The canonical tag named the bare form while the host's own
# redirect went the other way, so the two signals disagreed and a search engine was free to pick either -
# which is the arrangement that splits a page's signals between two addresses.
#
# www is the one Cloudflare serves as primary and the one the operator named, so it wins. 301 rather
# than 302 because this is permanent and should be cached as such.
#
# Order matters in a Cloudflare Pages _redirects file: the first matching rule wins, and these are
# placed before any catch-all. The splat carries the path and query through, so a deep link keeps its
# destination rather than landing on the homepage - the failure mode of a redirect written without one.
https://landedmath.com/* https://www.landedmath.com/:splat 301
